From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sinful1992 <sinful1992@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:26:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Binge-ahead: serve a prepared H.264 copy of the next episodes
 to devices that can't play them

A Fire TV Stick on the official app can't play HEVC Main 10, so every episode
of a show it binges is transcoded live (16 of 21 transcodes in a week, one
series in order). The order is predictable, and the server is idle at night.

When PlaybackInfo would transcode an episode for video reasons only, the
device and series are recorded (data/binge-ahead.json). The daily
"Binge-ahead" task (04:00, skipped while anything plays) prepares the next 2
unplayed episodes of those series whose video has the same codec/bit
depth/range: -map 0 -c copy -c:v:0 h264_vaapi, so every stream keeps its
index, and the result is discarded unless the stream layout matches.

The 0.19.11 app always asks for the original's media source id and composes
its own stream URL with no token or session id. So the prepared file is
answered under the original id as direct play, and that client's address is
remembered for the item for 12 hours; its static stream request is served
from the prepared file. Every other client and decision gets the original.
Prepared files are deleted once played or after 14 days, at most 4 kept.
